      "content_summary": "High-level troubleshooting guide for service unresponsiveness, HTTP 502 errors, and TLS handshake issues caused by network partitions, proxy misconfigurations, or certificate problems.",
      "content_body": "When users report timeouts or HTTP 502 errors, verify that the Load Balancer is correctly routing traffic to healthy backend instances. Check for network partition issues by ensuring that security groups or firewalls allow traffic on required ports. If TLS handshake errors or certificate warnings occur, inspect the certificate validity and expiration dates on the Session Controller. DNS lookup failures often stem from incorrect resolver configurations; ensure the server can resolve internal service names. Resolving these issues typically requires configuration changes, such as renewing expired certificates or correcting DNS entries."
